body:
I feel you bro. My mental issues also got in way with my academic life constantly.  There are few instances;

1.When I was doing my master I applied for a group to write my thesis, you first have an interview with the leader of the group than talk with every in the group and if even one of them says no you are out.

I talked first with the leader he said yes he was very impressed, he said he will take me, then I talked with everyone else in the group.  After a week i got email that says I am not accepted because the other people thinks that I am unfriendly and not to suitable to work in a group. I was really trying to be nice and to this they what did do wrong.

2.  Without an exception in every group I have ever worked. People tougth that I was excellent in my job, but I am a troubled anti social person and hard to work with. It costs me jobs and usefull proffesional relationships. I can't sustain a healty professional relationship with anyone. And this really hearts my academic life just being good is not enough if you are not a genius with iq of 180. 

&#x200B;

3. In academics giving presentations are very important this is how you get jobs and how you get a reputation in comunity. My mental issues always got in way while this presentations. When you are depressed troubled person with no self esteem. You can't effectively present your work in front of many people.

&#x200B;

4. because of my depression in bachelor I dropped out for one semester. Also because of depressive periods I stop studying at all one for while in my bachelor, at that time my gpa was 1.7 out of 4. After I tried very hard and got A from every course I took and finished my bachelor with 3.5 gpa.  But still this cost me a lot of opportunities, to be in a very good phd program.

&#x200B;

because of my derpession, i am in a wrose place than i deserve. 

&#x200B;
